func.func @main(%conv_transpose_weight: tensor<8x8x3x3xf32>, %conv_transpose_bias: tensor<8xf32>, %group_norm_weight: tensor<8xf32>, %group_norm_bias: tensor<8xf32>, %input: tensor<8x8x8x8xf32>) -> tensor<8x8x10x10xf32> {
  // conv_transpose_weight: [in_channels=8, out_channels=8, kernel_h=3, kernel_w=3]
  // input: [batch=8, in_channels=8, height=8, width=8]
  // We want to perform ConvTranspose2d with stride=1, kernel=3, groups=8
  // ConvTranspose2d is implemented as a convolution with lhs_dilation=stride and reversed kernel spatial dims.
  // The conv_transpose.weight shape is [in_channels, out_channels, kh, kw] in PyTorch,
  // but StableHLO convolution expects kernel shape [out_channels, in_channels/groups, kh, kw].
  // So we must transpose conv_transpose_weight from [8,8,3,3] to [8,1,3,3] per group, but groups=8 means each group has 1 in_channel and 1 out_channel.
  // Actually, groups=8 means feature_group_count=8, so input channels=8, output channels=8, each group has 1 channel.
  // So kernel shape for convolution: [out_channels=8, in_channels/groups=1, kh=3, kw=3]
  // We must reshape conv_transpose_weight from [8,8,3,3] to [8,1,3,3] by slicing or reshaping.
  // But conv_transpose_weight is [8,8,3,3], which is [in_channels, out_channels, kh, kw].
  // We need to transpose axes 1 and 0 to get [out_channels, in_channels, kh, kw], then reshape to [8,1,3,3].
  // Then set feature_group_count=8.

  // Step 1: transpose conv_transpose_weight from [8,8,3,3] (in_ch, out_ch, kh, kw) to [8,1,3,3] (out_ch, in_ch/group, kh, kw)
  // Actually, we want [out_ch=8, in_ch/group=1, kh=3, kw=3]
  // So first transpose axes 1 and 0: from (in_ch=8, out_ch=8, kh=3, kw=3) to (out_ch=8, in_ch=8, kh=3, kw=3)
  // Then slice to get in_ch/group=1 per group (groups=8), so for each out_ch, pick the corresponding in_ch in the group.
  // Because groups=8, each group has 1 in_ch and 1 out_ch, so for out_ch i, in_ch i is the only input channel.
  // So we slice the kernel to keep only the diagonal in the in_ch dimension.

  // Transpose conv_transpose_weight axes 1 and 0:
  %conv_weight_transposed = "stablehlo.transpose"(%conv_transpose_weight) {permutation = array<i64: 1, 0, 2, 3>} : (tensor<8x8x3x3xf32>) -> tensor<8x8x3x3xf32>

  // Now slice to keep only the diagonal in in_ch dimension (index i in in_ch dimension for out_ch i)
  // We'll do a dynamic slice per out_ch to get in_ch=1 slice at index i.
  // But dynamic_slice requires start indices as tensors, so we will do a loop unroll by reshape and gather.
  // Since stablehlo does not have gather, we simulate by dynamic_slice in a loop unrolled by 8 times.

  // Create constants for indices 0..7 for slicing
  %c0 = stablehlo.constant dense<0> : tensor<i32>
  %c1 = stablehlo.constant dense<1> : tensor<i32>
  %c2 = stablehlo.constant dense<2> : tensor<i32>
  %c3 = stablehlo.constant dense<3> : tensor<i32>
  %c4 = stablehlo.constant dense<4> : tensor<i32>
  %c5 = stablehlo.constant dense<5> : tensor<i32>
  %c6 = stablehlo.constant dense<6> : tensor<i32>
  %c7 = stablehlo.constant dense<7> : tensor<i32>

  // Slice sizes: [1,1,3,3] (in_ch dimension size 1)
